text.section:
Notwithstanding any other provision of law, motorcycles may be operated without headlights, horns, or rearview mirrors on public highways if all the following conditions are met:

The motorcycles are designed for use in trail riding and endurance runs;


The motorcycles are being driven by duly licensed persons;


The motorcycles are being operated between sunrise and sunset; and


The motorcycles are being operated during endurance runs sanctioned by the American Motorcycle Association.
